# End-to-end EMULATOR test: FYSETC Spider (STM32F446) under Renode in
# tick mode. Boots real firmware, completes identify + clocksync, brings
# up the full config (4 TMC2208s on dedicated single-wire UART pins,
# software-PWM heaters, fan, endstops, 2 thermistors) and round-trips
# M114/M105. See "Per-printer tests" in test/emulator/README.md for the
# shared conventions.
#
# Ground specific to this board:
#   - Single-wire-per-driver TMC2208 UART (PE7/PE15/PD10/PD7, rx == tx,
#     no datagram address), shared with skr_v1_4.test (LPC176x):
#     sw_uart keeps one state per pin and broadcasts the framed reply to
#     every registered RX pin. Here that drives the STM32 gpioPortE /
#     gpioPortD inputs via OnGPIO (skr_v1_4 drives LPC FIOPIN instead).
#   - The ADC needs no new stub: F4 shares src/stm32/adc.c and the
#     SR/CR2/SQR3/DR slice with F1, so stm32_adc_stub.py serves it. The
#     one difference - ADC_CR2 SWSTART at bit22 (F1) vs bit30 (F4) - is
#     absorbed inside the stub.
DICTIONARY stm32f446.dict
CONFIG fysetc_spider.cfg
EMULATOR fysetc_spider.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
